<div class="row mb-2">
    <div class="col-12">
        <div class="card border-danger shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-header bg-light text-danger fw-bold d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center">
                <span>
                    <i class="mdi mdi-information-outline me-2"></i> Penalty Configuration Guidelines
                </span>
                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#penaltyGuidelinesBody">
                    <i class="mdi mdi-chevron-down"></i>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div id="penaltyGuidelinesBody" class="collapse">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <ul class="mb-3 list-unstyled">

                        <!-- 🏷️ Penalty Type -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-format-list-bulleted-type text-primary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Penalty Type:</strong> Defines the logic to apply — use <code>Late_Repayment_Penalty</code> for installment defaults or <code>Penalty_After_Maturity_Date</code> for post-loan expiry.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 💵 Penalty Value -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-cash text-success me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Penalty Value:</strong> Enter a numeric amount. If <code>IsRate</code> is checked, this value is treated as a percentage of the base; otherwise, it is a flat fee.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🧮 Base Amount -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-calculator-variant-outline text-info me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Penalty Base:</strong> Choose from <code>Overdue_Principal_Amount</code>, <code>Overdue_Interest_Amount</code>, <code>Overdue_Daily_Interest_Amount</code>, or <code>Overdue_Principal_Plus_Interest</code>. Use <code>Apply_Fixed_Penalty_Amount</code> to apply fixed value directly.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⏱️ Grace Period -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-timer-sand-empty text-warning me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Grace Period:</strong> Defines the number of days after a due date before any penalty is considered. Helps protect compliant borrowers from accidental penalties.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⏲️ Apply After -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-calendar-clock text-info me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Apply After Days:</strong> Specifies how long after overdue the penalty should actually be enforced. Works in combination with Grace Period.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🔁 Recurrence -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-repeat text-primary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Recurrence Settings:</strong> Set <code>RecurringPeriod</code> (Days, Weeks, Months, Years) and <code>RecuringInterval</code> (e.g., 30) to determine how often the penalty should be reapplied. Applies only if <code>IsCumulative</code> is true.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 📌 Cumulative Logic -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-autorenew text-dark me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Cumulative Application:</strong> If <code>IsCumulative</code> is enabled, penalties will apply repeatedly as per recurrence settings. Disable to restrict application to once per cycle.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🔓 One-time Enforcement -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-lock-open-outline text-secondary me-2"></i>
                            <strong>One-Time Only:</strong> Set <code>IsOneTimeOnly</code> to true if this penalty must only apply once across the life of the loan. Often used for maturity or closure-related fees.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🚫 Max Cap -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-currency-usd-off text-danger me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Cap Amount:</strong> Use <code>PenaltyMaxCapAmount</code> to limit total charges from this rule. Prevents overcharging in long-term arrears.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⛔ Expiry -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-calendar-remove text-muted me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Auto Expire After:</strong> Use <code>HasExpiryAfterDays</code> and <code>ExpireAfterDays</code> to disable the rule automatically after a number of active days. Useful for promotional or transitional penalties.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 📆 Weekend Behavior -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-calendar-weekend-outline text-warning me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Weekend Enforcement:</strong> If <code>ApplyOnWeekends</code> is false, penalties will be skipped on Saturdays and Sundays. Enable for daily calculations.
                        </li>

                        <!-- 🏦 Posting Account -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-bank-outline text-dark me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Fee Posting:</strong> Use <code>FeePostingAccountId</code> to direct penalty revenue into a specific ledger or GL account.
                        </li>

                        <!-- ⚠️ Risk Warning -->
                        <li class="mb-2">
                            <i class="mdi mdi-alert-outline text-danger me-2"></i>
                            <strong>Important:</strong> Poorly configured penalties may result in excessive client burden, reputational damage, or compliance issues.
                        </li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr class="my-3" />

                    <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                        <i class="mdi mdi-help-circle-outline me-2"></i>
                        Always validate penalty logic with compliance, credit risk, and finance teams before activating on live loan products.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
